 lines += ['', 'Low/base/high are declared **historical all-candidate contest-volume anchors**:2022governor2,510,661;2024Senate3,189,323;2020Senate3,214,256. They are not estimated2026turnout, probability intervals, or the extrema of every possible source contest. Each of four preference anchors keeps its own county A/(A+B) and pair participation(A+B)/allCandidateVotes. Scenario T_county=historicalVolume_county*anchorParticipation_county. The remaining volume retains each named nonpair candidate’s anchor fraction. No candidate/coalition/lower-preference effect is inferred.','', 'The following holds2024Senate preferences and county pair participation fixed. Historical-mix runs change county volumes directly; fixed2024mix runs scale every county equally to the low/high statewide all-candidate total, isolating volume from composition. The same implementation saves every combination of four preference anchors, plus own-volume county/native/municipal runs:64state target runs,4,176county target rows,32,838native rows and22,098municipal rows. [State scenarios](data/baselines/state-scenarios.json), [full candidate scenarios](data/baselines/state-candidate-scenarios.csv), [native targets](data/baselines/native-targets.csv.gz), [municipal targets](data/baselines/municipal-targets.csv.gz).','', '|2024Senate preference setting|All candidate volume|Pair volume|Baseline DFL−R net|Tie shift share pp|A+1shift share pp|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
